````markdown
# Simple React

A lightweight React development scaffold built around Docker Compose.

The project is intended to provide a reusable starting point for React applications without having to recreate the development environment, container configuration, and basic project structure for every new project.

## Purpose

This repository acts as a base template for quickly starting React projects using Docker Compose.

Instead of installing and configuring the development environment separately for every project, the scaffold provides a containerized environment that can be cloned, renamed, and used as the foundation for a new application.

## Features

- React development environment
- Docker Compose based workflow
- Containerized Node.js environment
- Live development and hot reload
- Source code mounted from the host
- Isolated project dependencies
- Simple reusable project structure
- Minimal starting point without application-specific code

## Requirements

The host system only requires:

- Docker
- Docker Compose
- Git

Node.js and project dependencies are handled inside the container.

## Getting Started

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/tahasiraj97/simple-react.git
cd simple-react
```

Start the development environment:

```bash
docker compose up -d
```

Docker Compose will start the React development environment and install the required dependencies.

## Development

Source files can be edited directly from the host.

Changes to the React application are automatically detected by the development server, allowing the application to update without manually rebuilding the container.

View live container logs:

```bash
docker compose logs -f
```

View running services:

```bash
docker compose ps
```

## Rebuilding

If dependencies or container configuration are changed, rebuild the environment:

```bash
docker compose up -d --build
```

## Stopping the Environment

Stop and remove the running containers:

```bash
docker compose down
```

## Using as a Scaffold

This repository is intended to be reused as the starting point for other React projects.

A typical workflow is:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/tahasiraj97/simple-react.git my-project
cd my-project
rm -rf .git
git init
```

The scaffold can then be modified for the new application's requirements while retaining the existing Docker Compose development environment.

## Project Philosophy

The goal of this project is to keep React development environments simple and reproducible.

Application source code remains on the host while the runtime and dependencies remain inside Docker, allowing development to take place without installing or maintaining a separate Node.js environment on the host system.
````
